Z||000005||frontal lobe||05-05-2001||11:06 PM||||I am all for having a sense of humor, but you have to have some idea of when you are crossing the line.  And when you use small children in that manner, you simply have crossed the line.<P>You know what I always enjoy doing?  I enjoy explaining to my 6 year old who can now read anything--"Dad, what are titties?  And why would that boy want to drink beer?"<P>And while I am at it, a special thanks to all who have bumper stickers such as, "Don't like my driving?  Call 1-800-eat **** ."  Then I can answer questions like:  "Dad, what is **** ?  Well, why would someone want you to eat it?"<P>Final thought.  Was that picture taken outside an arena waiting to go into a WWF match where the little guy can watch 3/4 naked women taking the wrestlers to ringside and listen to his hero "the Rock" call someone a candy ass?||||reg||1
