Z||000011||Cheever2||05-06-2001||01:27 PM||||Frontal lobe, thank you.  I couldn't have said it better.  I'm appalled and disgusted by underachievers intentionally pushing their lack of taste & manners onto the rest of society.  Wouldn't be quite so bad if it wasn't exposed to the children, but it is.  It brings us all down as a civilization.  They call it freedom of speech, but it's really just losers who detest those with the self-discipline to make themselves a valuable member of the populace, the vision of the inividual's responsibility in holding up the human endeavor to excel, and keeping decency, cleanliness and initiative on a pedestal as something worth constantly striving for.  And we must strive for those things, because in our sinful human nature they don't come naturally.  Daily degradation is what comes naturally.  It's so easy for society to fall farther into a pit, but very difficult for it to rise and pull itself up by its bootstraps.  <P>I was born in 1957.  I remember when men wore ties in public, even to ballgames or just out shopping.  Sure there's nothing wrong with the freedom to wear T-shirts & jeans, various colors of hair, or body piercings if you want, that was a good result of the 60's and later years.  But people don't just value expression, they would rather push the envelope of decency and social acceptibility.  They don't just want to be <I>allowed</I> to do & say & look like they want, rather they insist on offending and trying their best to shock and disgust.  They wallow in the act of bringing others down to their level, and then finding new depths to descend.  They ridicule leaders, teachers, law makers and law enforcers, and those who attempt excellence in anything other than sports and entertainment.<P>That attitude is not only affecting our quality of life, but it's starting to affect our value of life itself.  If I get into that any further I know I'll bring on a whole new war here, but just think about what that means to <I>you</I>, and decide if you want to be part of the decline of the human existence, or if you will be one of the few who will help us all struggle for a higher aim, a better place for future generations.<P>(Editing because I didn't use the SpellChecker the first time)<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-08-2001).]||||reg||6
