Z||000017||frontal lobe||05-07-2001||01:34 AM||||Oh oh.  Time for some clarification.<P>To Tweek.  I didn't mean for you to edit out the picture.  I really didn't find it out of place in a car forum like this because the likelihood of small children winding up here is VERY small.  My kids didn't see it.  I was more speaking of what my experience over the last 9 years of having children and being out in public with them has been.  So to you again, I had NO problem with you posting it here.<P>To JohnnyK.  I am not a crazy father.  I also agree that he put it on his kid as a joke.  That was my point.  My opinion is that in attempting to go for the joke, using a child in that manner crossed the line of humor to being vulgar and offensive--not necessarily to all (such as yourself) but to a sizable portion of the population.  So much so that I wish he would have policed and governed HIMSELF and decided against a shirt like that in public.  But he didn't.  I don't want laws made against him doing it, though.  <P>To Pontiaddict.  "People have to learn about those things sometime..."  I always love that line.  Did you perhaps miss the fact that my daughter is SIX.  That was SIX. "Shielded from EVERYTHING their WHOLE life".  Love that line, too.  Where did I say THAT was the standard of shielding?   Yes, my daughters will need things explained to them and I do.  And how long, may I ask, did it take YOU to get up to speed on this kind of thing?  We generally are fast learners, so that if we don't get exposed to a bunch of garbage by age 12 or so, we can pick it up pretty fast.<P>Example.  Once I was taking the kids miniature golfing and there was a group of 19ish year olds right behind us.  They were loudly saying "f-this and f-ing that", repeatedly.  So I just KINDLY and politely ASKED them if they would consider watching their language as I had small children that I didn't prefer to explain that word to at this stage in life.  I don't think they were thinking about it, but when they did, they decided to not use those words.  But if they had, I would have just told the kids we had to leave and just left the place.  So THAT is how CRAZY I am, JohnnyK.||||reg||1
Z||000018||JSocha||05-07-2001||01:53 AM||||They have TV today to facilatate their training while we are at work from 6AM to midnight.<P>And then there are some parents that do take the time to teach their kids, and yes, some in a real disheartening way.<P>For example, like the time I went to the bathroom at a restraunt.<P>Standing there at the urinal when a little kid, about 5, 6 maybe even 8 went to the bathroom in the lowered kid's urinal next to me, did his business, zipped up and was heading out the bathroom door.<P>Me and my big trap, I said "Hey you!  Didn't your mom ever teach you to wash your hands after you pee?"<P>He turned around and responded "Didn't your mommy ever teach you not to p*ss on your hands?!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I guess I just led a sheltered life when I was young...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000019||firstfiero||05-07-2001||06:58 AM||||      okay....what is the big deal about that picture. sheeeesh you guys are touchy. <BR>      You don't like freedom of speech and expression? With everything your going to have a good side and a bad side. Example you have the right to watch the religious right...700 club... tell you how great god is and how bad gays are. On the other hand I have the right to watch porn until my hand falls off. There's an up side and down side of every freedom. If you want to wear a tie every day of your life...go head. I guess some how that makes you a better more evolved person because I enjoy wearing jeans and Tshirts. Does some how give some one more class. Maybe some people do like to intentionaly piss people off with the way they dress....how bout this don't give them the satisfaction. They'll grow up sooner or later. <BR>    By the way...yes I am a father of 2. 8 and 12. I have no problem explaining anything to them.  You explain the bumper sticker as a joke they'll get when they get older. That's the world we live in guys...if they don't learn from you trust me they'll learn it from the kids at school! ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Tweek||05-07-2001||04:17 PM||||frontal lobe, thanks for the explanation, I'm willing to bet the picture itself didn't offend 90% of anyone who saw it, but may have offended somebody. Though I do agree with the fact that our culture is so thoughtless and selfish and uncaring, that stuff like that and much worse is commonplace. I would have more to say but I think you guys have pretty much summed it up.||||reg||1
